# Pujo Sahayak — environment variables (copy to `.env.local` and fill in)
#
# Google Maps is OPTIONAL. With no key set, the "drop a pin" address picker
# falls back to the free, key-less Leaflet + OpenStreetMap implementation and
# everything works for anyone running the demo. Adding a real, billed key
# "lights up" the Google Maps picker — nothing is faked either way.
#
# To enable Google for the pin picker:
#   1. Google Cloud Console → create a project → enable billing (card on file).
#   2. Enable these APIs: "Maps JavaScript API" and "Geocoding API".
#   3. Credentials → create an API key → restrict it to your domain + those APIs.
#   4. Copy this file to `.env.local`, paste the key below, restart the dev server.
#
# Leave blank (or delete) to keep using the free OpenStreetMap picker.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=

#
# OpenAI is OPTIONAL and used only for Maya, the in-app chat guide.
# With no key set, Maya runs her on-device brain (~40 intents across pandals,
# routes, rituals, food, shopping, safety, Bengali) — no network, works fully
# offline, and answers stay grounded in the local dataset (no invented facts).
# Adding a real key "lights up" free-form chat: Maya starts hitting OpenAI
# Chat Completions with a strict Puja-focused system prompt + retrieved context.
# Anything off-topic is still declined in-character before the network call.
#
# To enable:
#   1. platform.openai.com → create a project → add billing.
#   2. Generate an API key → restrict to Chat Completions.
#   3. Copy this file to `.env.local`, paste the key below, restart the dev server.
#   4. For the APK, run `npm run build` + `npx cap sync android` AFTER setting
#      the key — env vars are baked at build time. This is intentional: keys
#      are NOT bundled when unset, so a public APK never leaks one.
#
# Optional override for the model name (defaults to gpt-4o-mini).
VITE_OPENAI_KEY=
VITE_OPENAI_MODEL=
